+### 4.1 AES-256 keys in stock CPS `.data` files
+
+The exact layout reported in [issue #42](https://github.com/donttellmeimcute/DM32-nxdn-p25/issues/42) has consecutive
+44-byte records starting at file offset `0xD300`. The slot is at byte 0, the 10-byte ASCII name at byte 1, the type at
+byte 11 and the 32 key octets at byte 12. Type `0x04` is AES-256. A record with an empty slot and erased filler ends
+the table. The converter only offers AES-256 records linked to an encrypted DMR channel, and it declines a malformed
+table or repeated slot. The file offset is specific to the reported export. The format of other versions remains open.
+
+Open a matching `.data` file in the Codeplug Editor. Enter the stock CPS **Encryption ID** for each key you want to
+migrate. The editor never uses the slot as the radio's key ID. The same confirmed ID is installed on every linked channel.
+Skipped keys and unsupported formats leave those channels receive-only. The automatic installer leaves them receive-only
+as well. **Write to radio** in the same session transfers the keys directly and keeps unrelated destination keys. A
+different AES-256 key at the same Encryption ID blocks the write. Drafts, exports and support attachments omit the keys.
+
