-## 8. Open points
+## 8. Local replay
+
+`CONFIG_DMR_REPLAY` uses a board-provided volatile buffer. The normal DMR sink stores corrected 49-bit AMBE frames
+in seven bytes each, with a lost-frame bit. The buffer holds 1,500 frames, the first 30 seconds of the most recent
+accepted clear group call whose opening header was received. Private calls, encrypted calls, and late entry are
+excluded. A privacy indication during recording discards the provisional recording. The audio path applies its normal
+loss concealment during local replay. The test-only voice capture does not provide or read this buffer.
+
+The session setting starts off. Disabling it, standby, power-off and initialization clear the buffer. The debug link
+refuses reads of the buffer, including overlapping reads. Replay runs through the existing AMBE RX queue and speaker
+route after verifying that the conventional DMR receiver is idle. Carrier, live voice, retune, PTT and automatic keying
+preempt the replay. Received RF and transmitted voice keep their normal paths and have priority over the clip.
+
