+### Startup PIN
+
+On a keypad radio that offers **Set or change startup PIN** under **Settings → My radio**, enter the same
+six digits twice. After the next power-on, enter that PIN and press **OK**. The radio and its host services
+start after the PIN is accepted. Changing or removing the PIN requires the current PIN. Three wrong attempts
+pause entry for 20 seconds. There is no default PIN.
+
+This is a local access lock. It does not encrypt the codeplug or protect memory from access outside the running
+firmware, such as the hardware bootloader. Keep your PIN somewhere you can recover it.
+
+After setting a startup PIN, use **Set or remove programming lock** in the same menu and confirm with the PIN.
+Reading, writing and backing up the codeplug through the running firmware then require a second local unlock.
+Choose **Unlock or relock programming**, enter the PIN on the radio and reconnect the computer.
+Choose that option again and enter the PIN to relock without restarting. Switching the radio off also relocks
+programming. Enter every PIN on the radio keypad. Host reads pause while the PIN prompt is open.
