+## Moving DMR AES-256 keys from the stock CPS
+
+Open the original Baofeng CPS `.data` file in the Web Codeplug Editor. If the file matches the reported stock key
+table, the editor lists the AES-256 rows linked to encrypted channels. In Baofeng CPS, look up each row under
+**Digital Encrypt Systems** and enter its **Encryption ID** from 1 to 255. Leave an ID blank to skip that key.
+Select **Import AES-256 keys**, review the channels and select **Write to radio** in the same session.
+
+Encrypted channels without an imported key stay receive-only. For a file whose layout differs, use **Radio → Keyring**
+to add the stock key manually, select its ID on the linked channels and clear **RX only** when you want to enable TX.
+Keep the original file private. Browser drafts and exported files omit the keys.
